{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For he was good</b> — יהוה — two tagin on the tet, one on the vav, two on the bet, to teach that he is destined to receive five books of Torah, as it is said of them: כי לקח טוב נתתי לכם." "<b>Months</b> — four times in the Masorah: here, and the other גרש ירחים, במספר ירחים אל יבוא, תספור ירח תמלאנה. As stated in the first chapter of Sotah: the Egyptians counted for her nine months from the day he returned her, and she had conceived three months before he divorced her — and this is תספור ירחים תמלאנה, they counted the months in order to know the time of her giving birth — במספר ירחים אל יבוא — and they could not know the number of months, for she had three months before he divorced her — and this is גרש ירחים — before he divorced her she already had months of pregnancy."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ה׳ תגין' appears to mean 'five tagin,' reading ה׳ as the number 5. Translated hyper-literally preserving the notation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:43.328434121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}